A sorter calls every message ordinary. Of 100 messages, 90 are ordinary and 10 are urgent.

```javascript
const correct = 90;
const total = 100;
const urgentFound = 0;
console.log(100 * correct / total);
console.log(urgentFound);
```

It prints 90, then 0. That is 90% accuracy while finding none of the urgent messages. These are recorded counts, not a running model.
